00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:18.140
- The opioid epidemic is
like nothing we've seen.

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:22.490
Each day it claims an average
of 130 lives in the US alone.

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:26.180
Its impact can be felt across
families and communities,

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:29.450
and it is being fought by first
responders, law enforcement,

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:31.190
and health care providers.

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:33.560
But its complexity
means no one group

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:35.930
is able to offer a
complete solution.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:38.960
To combat the opioid epidemic,
those at the front line

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:42.090
must be swift, deliberate,
and collaborative.

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:45.230
They need to intervene early
on to help focus resources

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.890
and protect lives.

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:49.950
They need to get to
the future faster.

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:53.420
That's why in collaboration
with Google and DataStax,

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:56.030
Deloitte has created
an analytic solution

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:59.930
for the people and organizations
responding to this challenge.

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:03.310
Opioid360 is sophisticated
and flexible,

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:06.860
synthesizing de-identified
data from disparate and siloed

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.830
sources and providing
insight into the crisis

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:11.870
like never before.

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:13.720
And it leverages
our deep experience

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:16.210
with AI and predictive
modeling, helping

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:19.990
your organization take the
right action at the right time.

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:22.720
Imagine those on the
front being able to dial

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:25.270
into the needs of
specific populations.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:28.210
Imagine the risk of addiction
mapped against barriers

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:30.640
to treatment, such
as housing security,

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:34.630
unreliable transportation,
or lack of insurance.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:37.450
Imagine all of this
powered by a dedication

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:40.405
to privacy and security and
the empathetic knowledge

00:08:40.405 --> 00:08:43.090
that the people are
more than data sets.

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:45.670
People require
tailored interventions,

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:47.980
ones that match
their medical needs

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:51.490
and address any barriers to
care, like transportation

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:54.580
assistance for Chris so he
can get to his local treatment

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:57.160
facility, or the
support Maria needs

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:59.920
to keep her family of four
together while she receives

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:03.800
treatment, and information
for Alex's medical provider

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:05.830
so he can make the
best choice about how

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:08.140
to manage Alex's back pain.

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:11.440
We don't have one opioid
epidemic, but many,

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.120
striking in tandem.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:17.260
With Opioid360, we gain
much needed visibility.

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:20.860
Its predictive models help
identify at-risk populations

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:23.590
and treatment barriers
earlier in the lifecycle,

00:09:23.590 --> 00:09:26.740
leading to timely,
proven interventions,

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:29.050
and its flexibility
makes it a viable tool

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:31.510
for each of the multiple
organizations trying

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:35.660
to solve this complex, costly,
and interconnected problem.

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:40.150
A future with lowered rates of
opioid misuse can start today.

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:41.995
It's time for Opioid360.

